        "titulo": "THE BIG SURPRISE: the words where «it» in English hides a gender",
        "explicacao": "THE BIG SURPRISE: the words where «it» in English hides a gender. This section is usually missing from grammars, but it is the one you will use most. English has «he», «she» and «it», and for things you always say «it». Your brain has an autopilot: a book, a car, a table are all «it». In Russian, that autopilot lets you down, because every one of those things is secretly masculine, feminine or neuter, and nothing in English tells you which. Do not assume that «it» means neuter. Neuter is just one of three boxes: a car is feminine, a table is masculine, a window is neuter. The only reliable guide is the ending. Here are the common words English speakers get wrong at first: Learn these. They will save you months of confusion. These are the words that appear most in beginner texts. Learn them.",
